WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Autopsy reports usually confirm what's already&nbsp;
known about a celebrity's death. But some reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.140
secrets that the public — and in at least one&nbsp;
case, the celebrity themself — may not have known.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.820
"Just take a look at these fans who spent the&nbsp;
night out here mourning the loss of Paul Walker."

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.500
Paul Walker died as a passenger in a car driven&nbsp;
by his friend Roger Rodas on November 30,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.480
2013. The vehicle collided with a lamp post and&nbsp;
two trees in the San Fernando Valley suburb of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.800
Valencia, California. After striking the&nbsp;
second tree, the car burst into flames,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.300
and both Walker and Rodas were declared dead&nbsp;
by Los Angeles County firefighters who arrived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.620
on the scene. While it was believed that Walker&nbsp;
died as a result of the collision, a report from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.180
the Los Angeles County Coroner showed that the&nbsp;
40-year-old suffered a far more agonizing fate.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:46.412
As the report reveals, his body was found&nbsp;
lying across the passenger seat of the car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:51.240
Walker had suffered extensive "thermal injuries,"&nbsp;
including charred skin and fractured bones that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.380
according to the medical examiner, were&nbsp;
heat-related. Soot was found in his trachea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.980
which indicated that he was able to breathe,&nbsp;
and was therefore alive, while the car was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:04.860
on fire. His bloodstream also had 14% carbon&nbsp;
monoxide saturation — 12% higher than normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.190
levels. The report ultimately cited traumatic and&nbsp;
thermal injuries as the cause of Walker's death.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:15.060
It was a tragic end to an acclaimed career:&nbsp;
Oscar-winning actor Philip Seymour Hoffman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:20.760
was found dead from a drug overdose at the age of&nbsp;
46 on February 2, 2014. As his longtime partner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.320
costume designer Mimi O'Donnell noted in an essay&nbsp;
for Vogue, Hoffman had struggled with substance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.940
abuse during his college years. After that, he&nbsp;
remained sober for decades before experiencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.800
several personal struggles that led to a relapse,&nbsp;
followed by a return to treatment in 2013.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.600
In late February 2014, the New York Medical&nbsp;
Examiner's Office issued its findings in a report,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.920
which stated that Hoffman's death was the&nbsp;
result of an accidental overdose caused by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.260
acute mixed drug intoxication. A combination of&nbsp;
various narcotics, including heroin, cocaine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:53.340
amphetamines, and benzodiazepines, may have&nbsp;
been taken sequentially in a relatively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.300
short period. Chronic drug users may not&nbsp;
feel the immediate effects of substances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.780
so they will mix more drugs in order&nbsp;
to produce a high. As chief medical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:05.000
correspondent for CNN Dr. Sanjay&nbsp;
Gupta said in a 2014 interview,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.440
"They're not feeling it, but it's&nbsp;
still having an impact on their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.000
ability to breathe, and that's the real problem."

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:16.020
On January 9, 2022, comedian and "Full House"&nbsp;
star Bob Saget was found unresponsive in a hotel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.100
room in Orlando, Florida. The 65-year-old&nbsp;
was pronounced dead on the scene of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.580
was initially reported to be blunt-force&nbsp;
trauma to the head. The Orange County&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.600
Sheriff's Office conducted an investigation&nbsp;
and relayed their findings to Saget's family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.169
who issued a statement in February&nbsp;
of that year. The family wrote.

00:02:30.169 --> 00:02:33.960
"They have concluded that he accidentally&nbsp;
hit the back of [his] head on something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.863
thought nothing of it, and went to sleep."

00:02:35.863 --> 00:02:40.200
His family went on to clarify that no drugs&nbsp;
or alcohol were involved. The New York Times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.783
also noted that the sheriff's office&nbsp;
dismissed any suggestion of foul play.

00:02:43.783 --> 00:02:48.300
The autopsy report gave a more detailed account&nbsp;
of the extent of Saget's injuries. Dr. Joseph&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.740
Stephany, the chief medical examiner for Orange&nbsp;
and Osceola counties, wrote that he suffered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:57.060
a serious blow to the head — one that caused&nbsp;
fractures to the back, right side, and front&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:01.440
of his skull. The blow also led to vein rupture,&nbsp;
which caused blood to pool in the space between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:05.640
the brain and the surrounding membrane. Stephany&nbsp;
concluded that the injuries were most likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.840
caused by a fall, though a New York Times article&nbsp;
shared observations from medical professionals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.100
who questioned the idea that Saget would have&nbsp;
gone to sleep after experiencing such an injury.

00:03:14.562 --> 00:03:19.860
On March 23, 2016, Emmy-winning comedian Garry&nbsp;
Shandling told a doctor friend that he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.060
experiencing pain in his legs and shortness of&nbsp;
breath. The friend advised him to seek medical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:28.200
attention, but Shandling was hesitant. When his&nbsp;
condition failed to improve the following day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.700
Shandling called 911 and collapsed during the&nbsp;
call. He was rushed to St. John's Hospital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.780
in Santa Monica, California, where he&nbsp;
was pronounced dead at the age of 66.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.123
"Garry is gone, and this just doesn't seem real."

00:03:40.123 --> 00:03:43.980
Shandling's death was initially reported as&nbsp;
a heart attack, but the Los Angeles County&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:48.660
Coroner's Office opened an investigation to&nbsp;
determine the actual cause. The office issued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:54.060
their findings in December 2016, which noted that&nbsp;
a toxicology report found only therapeutic amounts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:58.980
of Xanax and opiates in his system, which, as&nbsp;
TMZ noted, were prescribed for then-recent dental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.180
work. The report also found that Shandling&nbsp;
had died from a pulmonary embolism caused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.800
by a blood clot in his lungs. The clot, also&nbsp;
known as deep vein thrombosis, developed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.460
his legs during a trip to Hawaii, which was&nbsp;
when he had first reported feeling unwell.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:16.020
According to the Centers for Disease Control and&nbsp;
Prevention, blood clots can form when individuals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:20.220
must travel while sitting in a confined space,&nbsp;
such as a flight. In many cases, the clots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:24.360
dissolve on their own, but some break apart and&nbsp;
move to the lungs, causing a pulmonary embolism.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.860
Actor Tyler Sanders' impressive list of&nbsp;
television credits included a starring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:33.600
role on the Amazon series "Just Add Magic:&nbsp;
Mystery City" and guest appearances on "9-1-1:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.560
Lone Star" and "Fear the Walking Dead" —&nbsp;
all of which he'd achieved while still a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.060
teenager. Unfortunately, Sanders also struggled&nbsp;
with both depression and substance abuse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.840
the latter of which contributed to&nbsp;
his untimely death at the age of 18.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:51.720
Sanders was found dead in his Los Angeles home on&nbsp;
June 16, 2022. Six months later, the Los Angeles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.340
Department of Medical Examiner-Coroner issued&nbsp;
its findings. The report noted that Sanders had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.820
a history of drug use, and that he had informed&nbsp;
a friend the night before his death that he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.840
reported using fentanyl. The same friend found&nbsp;
Sanders at his home and called paramedics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.312
who pronounced the actor dead. Drug paraphernalia&nbsp;
was visible and identified at the scene.

00:05:08.312 --> 00:05:12.420
Medical examiner Robyn Parks wrote in the&nbsp;
report that fentanyl, which is a synthetic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:18.000
opioid, can be 50 to 100 times as potent as the&nbsp;
pharmaceutical painkiller morphine. She concluded,

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.020
"Based on the history, circumstances,&nbsp;
and examination as I currently know them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.060
the manner of death is accidental."

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:29.640
On August 5, 2022, Daytime Emmy-winning actor&nbsp;
Anne Heche was involved in a series of vehicular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.420
accidents before colliding with a house that&nbsp;
caused both the car she was driving and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:37.860
building to catch fire. It took firefighters&nbsp;
45 minutes to extricate Heche from the vehicle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:41.220
during which she suffered both&nbsp;
severe burns and smoke inhalation.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.760
"And even if they'd known for certain&nbsp;
someone was in the wrecked car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.453
it probably would not have changed what happened."

00:05:47.453 --> 00:05:51.780
Treatment at an area hospital and burn center&nbsp;
revealed that the extent of the damage included a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:56.760
traumatic brain injury. After lapsing into a coma,&nbsp;
Heche was declared legally dead on August 11.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:00.300
Law enforcement officials stated at the&nbsp;
time of the accident that Heche was under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.500
the influence of narcotics, and a preliminary&nbsp;
blood analysis appeared to show the presence of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.760
cocaine and other substances in her system.&nbsp;
However, a report issued on December 6,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:13.200
2022 from the Los Angeles County Department&nbsp;
of Medical Examiner-Coroner revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.040
only an inactive element of cocaine and&nbsp;
marijuana were found in her system. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.800
meant that she had not used either&nbsp;
substance at the time of the crash.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.580
The official cause of death was listed&nbsp;
as smoke inhalation and thermal injuries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:28.860
with first-degree burns covering over 40% of her&nbsp;
body. Heche also suffered a sternal fracture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.780
which made it difficult for her to breathe and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.960
according to the coroner's office,&nbsp;
contributed significantly to her death.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:39.900
Fans of Anton Yelchin were stunned by news of the&nbsp;
"Star Trek" actor's death in 2016. The young star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.800
died after his own car pinned him against a&nbsp;
security fence at his home in Studio City,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:48.480
California. A police investigation and subsequent&nbsp;
report from the Los Angeles County Coroner's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:52.560
office found that the 27-year-old actor died&nbsp;
as a result of blunt traumatic asphyxia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.660
or intense compression of his chest. The report&nbsp;
suggested that at 1 a.m. on June 19, 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:02.700
Yelchin may have stepped out of his 2015 Jeep&nbsp;
Grand Cherokee to check his gate or mail. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:06.900
vehicle, which was parked on a steep incline on&nbsp;
his driveway, may not have been properly parked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.320
and it rolled backward, crushing him&nbsp;
against a brick fence pillar and the gate.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:14.040
The report stated that Yelchin's death was&nbsp;
accidental and took place within a minute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:20.040
after the car struck him. CBS News noted in&nbsp;
2016 that 850,000 vehicles — the majority of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:25.200
which were 2014 and 2015 Jeep Grand Cherokees —&nbsp;
were under investigation by the National Highway&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:29.880
Traffic Safety Administration because of their&nbsp;
electronic gearshift. Yelchin's family settled a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:34.500
wrongful death lawsuit against Fiat Chrysler&nbsp;
Automobiles for undisclosed terms in 2018.

00:07:34.778 --> 00:07:39.540
The legacy of the popular, Emmy-winning musical&nbsp;
comedy-drama series "Glee" was tempered by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:43.380
the fact that three of its cast members&nbsp;
died. Naya Rivera was one of those actors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.980
who played cheerleader Santana Lopez&nbsp;
on the series. She died while spending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:51.000
time with her four-year-old son at&nbsp;
California's Lake Piru on July 8, 2020.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:54.840
A report from the Ventura County Medical&nbsp;
Examiner revealed that Rivera and her son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:59.760
Josey, were swimming in Lake Piru. After helping&nbsp;
her son back into their rented boat, Rivera was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:04.140
unable to return to the craft. The report stated&nbsp;
that her son saw her struggle and call for help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:09.300
before disappearing into the water; her body&nbsp;
was found five days later on July 13, 2020.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.920
According to the report, Rivera suffered from&nbsp;
vertigo and had small amounts of the anti-anxiety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:18.300
medication diazepam in her system, along with&nbsp;
an appetite suppressant. Neither of these was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:22.800
cited as a factor in her death, however, which was&nbsp;
instead attributed solely to accidental drowning.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.000
Actor Michael K. Williams overcame a&nbsp;
debilitating struggle with substance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:30.720
abuse to become a powerful presence in&nbsp;
numerous acclaimed television series. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:34.140
is known for roles like the vengeful Omar&nbsp;
Little in "The Wire," powerful gangster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:37.440
Albert "Chalky" White in "Boardwalk&nbsp;
Empire," and his Emmy-nominated turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:41.820
as Montrose Freeman in "Lovecraft Country."&nbsp;
Williams was also dedicated to supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:46.140
individuals — especially young people — through&nbsp;
nonprofits like his Making Kids Win initiative.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:51.240
"Why is this not here for my young people,&nbsp;
my children. There's nothing for them to do."

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.840
Additionally, he explored the circumstance&nbsp;
that often brought young people to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.480
drug trade and juvenile justice&nbsp;
system through Emmy-nominated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.780
documentaries like the Vice News&nbsp;
series "Black Market." Tragically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:05.700
Williams was found dead at the age of 54 in&nbsp;
his Brooklyn apartment on September 6, 2021.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:09.360
A report from the New York City Office&nbsp;
of the Chief Medical Examiner found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.260
that Williams had died of acute drug&nbsp;
intoxication after using heroin laced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:16.920
with the synthetic opioid fentanyl&nbsp;
and an analog, parafluorofentanyl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.297
His death was ruled accidental. Fans and&nbsp;
co-stars alike paid tribute to Williams.

00:09:21.297 --> 00:09:25.500
In 2023, the U.S. Attorney's Office for the&nbsp;
Southern District of New York reported that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:29.100
Irvin Cartagena, part of the drug trafficking&nbsp;
organization that sold heroin to Williams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:32.400
pleaded guilty to charges of&nbsp;
conspiring to distribute narcotics.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:37.920
Authorities were called to the home of Cameron&nbsp;
Boyce on the afternoon of July 6, 2019, after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:43.020
the actor was found unresponsive. Boyce, who was&nbsp;
best known for shows such as "Jessie" and Disney's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:47.520
"Descendants," was pronounced dead on the scene,&nbsp;
shocking fans and co-stars alike. While tributes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:52.440
poured in on social media, the Los Angeles County&nbsp;
Coroner's Office performed an autopsy. Officials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:56.100
were reluctant to release a cause of death&nbsp;
due to a need for "further investigation."

00:09:56.100 --> 00:10:01.380
The coroner's report, issued on July 30, 2019,&nbsp;
noted that Boyce suffered from epilepsy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:05.220
that his death was natural and caused by a&nbsp;
seizure related to the condition. A statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:09.000
from his family corroborated that finding,&nbsp;
adding that he died in his sleep from Sudden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.080
Unexpected Death in Epilepsy. According to the&nbsp;
Centers for Disease Control and Prevention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:16.260
this little-known condition affects&nbsp;
approximately one out of every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:21.840
1,000 individuals with epilepsy. The exact cause&nbsp;
is not known, but the CDC explains that death may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:25.380
occur when a seizure causes an interruption&nbsp;
to breathing patterns or heart rhythm.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:30.180
South African model turned actor Charlbi&nbsp;
Dean was on the brink of stardom thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:34.680
to a role in the 2022 Palme d'Or-winning&nbsp;
film "Triangle of Sadness." But her ascent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:38.880
was cut short on August 29, 2022, when&nbsp;
her representation reported that she had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:42.720
died of a sudden and unexpected illness&nbsp;
at a New York City hospital. Her cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:46.320
of death wasn't revealed until December of&nbsp;
that year when a spokesperson from the New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:50.400
York Medical Examiner's Office stated that&nbsp;
the 32-year-old died of bacterial sepsis.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.840
The examiner's office revealed that Dean, who&nbsp;
also had a recurring role as Syonide on "Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:59.880
Lightning" had been infected by Capnocytophaga,&nbsp;
a bacterium commonly found in both animals and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:04.140
humans. The bacteria is related to a variety&nbsp;
of health problems, and in certain cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:08.760
it can cause serious illnesses. The examiner's&nbsp;
office reported that the sepsis occurred because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:13.740
Dean was vulnerable to infections after having&nbsp;
her spleen removed following a 2009 car accident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:18.660
in Cape Town. That same accident also left her&nbsp;
with multiple broken bones and a collapsed lung.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:22.860
The circumstances surrounding the&nbsp;
1981 death of Natalie Wood continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:27.180
to fascinate classic Hollywood and true&nbsp;
crime devotees alike. The Oscar-nominated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:31.020
actor drowned while on a boat trip with&nbsp;
her husband Robert Wagner on November 29,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:36.840
1981. An autopsy report issued at the time by&nbsp;
Los Angeles County coroner Thomas Noguchi cited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:41.100
accidental drowning and hypothermia as the&nbsp;
cause of her death. The report also noted,

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:45.060
"Superficial skin bruises on the extremities&nbsp;
and abrasions on the left side of her face."

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:48.840
These were attributed to injuries sustained&nbsp;
at the time of Wood's drowning. A number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:52.140
of prescription drugs were found in her&nbsp;
system, including the painkiller Darvon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:56.340
medication to combat seasickness and&nbsp;
insomnia, and two unidentified pills.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:12:00.540
The superficial injuries on Wood's body remained&nbsp;
a pressing question for those who believed there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.960
was more to her demise than drowning. When&nbsp;
the Los Angeles County Sheriff's Office&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:08.580
reopened the inquiry in 2011, these bruises&nbsp;
and other marks were suggested as supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:12.180
evidence that Wood may have been injured&nbsp;
prior to entering the water. As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:16.740
the cause of death was changed to "drowning&nbsp;
and other undetermined factors," though no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:20.160
conclusive evidence of another cause&nbsp;
was, or has yet to be presented.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:27.900
"Natalie Wood was also loved by a world-full&nbsp;
of audiences, and they too, will miss her."

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:31.740
Cult movie fans remember actor Yvette&nbsp;
Vickers as the star of such '50s science&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:36.060
fiction favorites as "Attack of the 50-Foot&nbsp;
Woman" and "Attack of the Giant Leeches." The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:40.260
actor and former Playboy Playmate achieved&nbsp;
a greater if more tragic notoriety in death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:44.760
when she was found at her Beverly Hills home&nbsp;
on April 27, 2011. A concerned neighbor who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:48.480
noted that the 82-year-old Vickers had not&nbsp;
been seen for several months entered the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:52.380
actor's house and found her remains, which&nbsp;
were in an advanced state of decomposition.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:56.880
According to a report by the Los Angeles County&nbsp;
Coroner's Office, the cause of Vickers' death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:01.080
was heart disease. However, the body was so&nbsp;
decomposed that the coroner's office described&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:05.640
it as appearing to be mummified. In fact, it was&nbsp;
in a state of decay so advanced that initially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:09.360
it was impossible to determine whether&nbsp;
the body was male or female. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:13.560
dental records helped to confirm that the body&nbsp;
was that of Vickers, but the exact date of death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:18.964
was impossible to determine. Lt. Tony Carranza of&nbsp;
the Los Angeles Police Department told ABC News,

00:13:18.964 --> 00:13:20.520
"Once you start to have decomposition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:24.738
it becomes more difficult but it looks like&nbsp;
it's probably six months; it's hard to say."

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:29.520
Fans of Stephen "tWitch" Boss experienced&nbsp;
shock and dismay upon learning of his death by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:34.620
self-inflicted gunshot wound. According to the Los&nbsp;
Angeles County Medical Examiner's report, no other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:39.847
factors contributed to his death on December&nbsp;
13, 2022, which was confirmed as a suicide.

00:13:39.847 --> 00:13:44.280
The 40-year-old dancer and "Ellen DeGeneres&nbsp;
Show" DJ did not have any drugs or alcohol in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:49.080
his system and his body showed no other signs&nbsp;
of trauma or wounds. Additionally, Boss' wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:53.040
dancer and choreographer Allison Holker,&nbsp;
told law enforcement that her husband did not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:57.900
have a "history of suicide attempts or suicidal&nbsp;
ideation." She also confirmed that he did not have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:02.905
any mental health problems or financial or marital&nbsp;
issues that might have contributed to his suicide.

00:14:02.905 --> 00:14:07.045
"Stephen was an incredible father&nbsp;
and an incredible husband."

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.620
A frequent guest star and recurring&nbsp;
player on numerous television series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:16.260
actor Heath Freeman appeared on "ER," "NCIS," and&nbsp;
"Without a Trace." He also enjoyed a three-episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:21.660
arc between 2005 and 2007 as the sadistic&nbsp;
serial killer Howard Epps on "Bones." Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:26.880
Freeman earned more headlines for his untimely&nbsp;
death at the age of 41 on November 14, 2021.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:31.740
The actor was pronounced dead after being found&nbsp;
unresponsive in his home in Austin, Texas. Several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:35.880
months later, the Travis County Medical Examiner&nbsp;
made public its findings in an autopsy report.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:41.340
TMZ published the report on March 9, 2022, which&nbsp;
revealed that he died of a combination of alcohol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:45.900
narcotics, and prescription medication. Among&nbsp;
the drugs found in Freeman's system at the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:51.060
of the autopsy were fentanyl, cocaine,&nbsp;
oxycodone, hydrocodone, and alprazolam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:54.900
which is better known by the name brand,&nbsp;
Xanax. The report also noted that police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:59.580
discovered both Xanax and oxycodone pills&nbsp;
at Freeman's home. Opiates like oxycodone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:03.900
and benzodiazepines like Xanax are dangerous and&nbsp;
potentially lethal when combined with alcohol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

